Training data: Internet Archive scans
-------------------------------------

Training lines were also cut from these Internet Archive items
(https://archive.org/details/<identifier>), scans of public-domain books
made by the university libraries named below. They were fetched from the
Internet Archive (its metadata and IIIF services), the route HeOCR's legal
strategy calls internet_archive. The Internet Archive publishes them without
an explicit licence: none carries a licenseurl or rights field (source class
ia_library_scan_no_licence_field). The original conditions of each item on
the Internet Archive still apply. None was digitized by Google, and none
comes from NLI.

Each item passed HeOCR's Internet Archive rights gate
(hocrgen.fetchers.ia_iiif.decide_ia_rights; hocrgen decision
planning/decisions/2026-11-09-internet-archive-library-scans.md), and each
Ben-Yehuda work aligned to it has its own rights justification
(hocrgen.rights_justification.v1; hocrgen decision
planning/decisions/2026-11-10-legal-strategy.md). In short: a public-domain
book, a faithful scan by the named library, fetched from the Internet
Archive; no new right arises in the scan and no contract binds its reuse.
The justification ids are listed in r7_training_run.json. Death years are
the ones those justifications record.

