No checkpoint-selection line comes from the Internet Archive.

Every author, translator, editor and other named contributor of the books
above died more than 70 years ago, so the books are in the public domain in
Israel. Every book except Shirim was printed before 1931 and is also past
the United States copyright term. The US status of Shirim (1938, one
training line) is not established.

The model contains no scan images. The line crops are not distributed with
it.

Training data: text
-------------------

Each training line is labelled with the transcription of the same edition
from Project Ben-Yehuda (https://benyehuda.org), public domain dump release
2026-03 (https://github.com/projectbenyehuda/public_domain_dump). Its
licence states that the data files are in the public domain. Credit: Project
Ben-Yehuda volunteers.

Evaluation data (not used for training)
---------------------------------------

The model was scored on 38 page transcriptions from Hebrew Wikisource
(https://he.wikisource.org), licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike licence (CC BY-SA), as adjudicated by HeOCR's human
reviewers. They were used only to score the model after it was chosen,
never for training, tuning or checkpoint selection. The model contains no
Wikisource text.

